# a test run has opened a name on Object.prototype. An accessor that is laid there is handed what the read is asked of, and what it stores into a copy of the object is lost to the next read of the object
# so no copy stands for the object, and the read stays as it is written
# function pick() { return arguments[key]; }   Object.defineProperty(Object.prototype, "poke", { get() { this[0] = 9; return 0; } })
